    {
      "id": "claim_f4dd390009e645ce83c29cac89fa05df",
      "statement": "The ApprovalQueue contract: observations must be authorized before data is returned to the caller (fetching first is fine as long as the operation is read-only and authorization precedes any data crossing back), every side-effecting action must be submitted and must not be performed until applyAction is called (there is no mode where skipping the check is OK), and gatekeepers are encouraged to simulate unapproved actions so reads reflect them — letting the agent continue and the user batch-approve later instead of stalling synchronously.",
