      "id": "claim_f84340fd326e40298729cb4a02acbac8",
      "statement": "applyPendingAction is the single chokepoint where an action transitions to approved, requiring resolvedBy and autoApproved so no apply path can omit how the gate was cleared (the audit log always records the resolving user and whether it was automatic); manual approval resolves the approver's profile BEFORE applying so a failed profile fetch cannot leave an action applied in the world but still pending in storage.",
